<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banias</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paneas, Caesarea Philippi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caesarea Philippi was an ancient city at the springs of the Jordan below <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-hermon">Mount Hermon</a>, on the site of the shrine of Pan at Paneas. Herod's son Philip the Tetrarch rebuilt it around 2 BCE and made it his capital, naming it after Augustus. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agrippa-ii">Agrippa II</a> later renamed it Neronias, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a> place Peter's confession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> near it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banias.jpg" alt="Banias" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gugganij · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banias_Spring_Cliff_Pan%27s_Cave.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
